From 6f989280cb364d03ca1ea64b790223cf83258c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yangtse Su <yangtsesu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:57:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(core): resolve missing text deltas through font
 advances

An OFD text run that declares no `DeltaX` for a scalar is positioned by that
scalar's font advance, which is what the renderer draws. The semantic text
index, however, advanced such scalars by the font size, so page geometry
drifted away from the glyphs: on a 22-character Latin line at size 3 mm the
character boxes spread over 63 mm while the drawn text was 28 mm wide, and a
search rectangle for a match late in the line fell to the right of the text it
belonged to. Consumers that draw from this geometry - search highlights,
selection, caret and hit-testing - therefore looked misplaced on any document
whose producers rely on font metrics instead of explicit deltas.

The core crate still does not touch fonts. `TextAdvanceProvider` lets a caller
supply the per-scalar advances, `Document::from_bytes_with_advances` /
`open_with_advances` carry a provider into the page text index, and without one
the previous font-size footprint stays in place (and stays flagged
conservative). rofd-render implements the provider over exactly the resolution
and advance code the positioner uses, exposing the advance each positioned glyph
contributed so the two layers cannot drift apart. rofd-ffi loads documents with
the default font stack, which is what a renderer created with NULL options uses.

Verified: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo clippy -p rofd-core -p rofd-render
-p rofd-ffi --all-targets -- -D warnings; cargo test for the three crates;
crates/rofd-ffi/tests/run_c_tests.sh (symbol list, C/C++ headers, smoke). New
tests cover the provider seam in the core builder (including explicit deltas
staying authoritative and a provider that cannot resolve a font), the
provider/positioner agreement on an embedded subset font, and the ABI's layout
and search rectangles following font metrics.
